## Conventions
- You must follow all existing code conventions used in this application. When creating or editing a file, check sibling files for the correct structure, approach, and naming.
- Use descriptive names for variables and methods. For example, `isRegisteredForDiscounts`, not `discount()`.
- Check for existing components to reuse before writing a new one.

## Verification Scripts
- Verify on the real thing (the flow end to end, a read-only query on the data); tests, when written, are E2E only (see the top of this file).

## Application Structure & Architecture
- Stick to existing directory structure; don't create new base folders without approval.
- Add or change a dependency only as convention 6 allows (root `CLAUDE.md`): a package that passes its maintenance check is added without asking.

## Frontend Bundling
<!-- unless:spa -->
- If a frontend change doesn't show in the UI or you get a "Unable to locate file in Vite manifest" error, the Vite dev server in the local Docker stack may be down, or a production bundle needs `{{ $assist->nodePackageManagerCommand('run build') }}` (root `CLAUDE.md`, Hosting). Ask them.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
- If a frontend change doesn't show in the UI, the SvelteKit dev server (the stack's `vite` program) may be down; the production build is `npm run build` in `frontend/` (`frontend/CLAUDE.md`). Ask them.
<!-- endif -->

## Documentation Files
- You must only create documentation files if explicitly requested by the user.
